# Copy to .dockerignore in a PHP web application (drez-containerize skill, PHP track).
# The PHP Dockerfile copies the whole folder, so this list is the only thing
# keeping data, written configuration and secrets out of the image.
# In .dockerignore "*.db" matches only at the top of the folder; "**/*.db"
# matches at any depth. Keep the "**/" on every file pattern.
.git
.github
reference
data
backups
logs
tools/php
tests
.claude
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.mdf
**/*.ldf
**/*.bak
**/config.php
**/config.local.php
**/.installed
**/*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*-DESKTOP-*
**/*.docx
**/*.pdf
**/*.xlsx
**/config.local.json
**/config.local.json.tmp
.cache
dist
Migration
# Apache serves every file under the document root, so nothing but the
# application may enter the image (found in the build rehearsal, 2026-10-13):
# agent notes, handoffs, Windows launchers and the demo seeder stay out.
# tools/migrate.php, roles.php, pg-*.php stay for docker exec; each refuses a
# web request. tools/config.php has no such guard and only edits
# config.local.json, which the image never holds.
docs
scripts
**/*.md
**/*.bat
**/*.exe
**/*.ps1
launcher
launcher-stop
tools/check.js
tools/config.php
seed-demo.php
hardcoded-allow.json
env.template.txt
config.template.json
Dockerfile
compose.yaml
.dockerignore
.gitignore
.gitattributes
